LineComment   "// optional<T> is the prelude's name for a value that may be absent: the generic"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// alias `type optional<T> = T | null`. It is an alias, not a wrapper — it carries"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// no tag of its own, so it behaves in every respect exactly like the bare union"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// T | null it stands for. A member value and the null literal both assign to it,"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// match narrows it, and exhaustiveness sees through it. This example folds that"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// flow end to end over optional<nint>."
Newline       "\n"
Newline       "\n"
